&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Technology Infrastructure team operates globally and is responsible for every aspect of the firm&#39;s hybrid platform. This ranges from our EUC/Office environments to Trading and Core service Co-Location Data Centres, and extends to Public Cloud, delivering top-tier technology services to a dynamic and demanding Trading organisation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition to meeting the round-the-clock operational demands of the platforms, we continuously evolve and transform our platforms to maintain a competitive edge that our business requires. We innovate to provide valuable solutions and leverage our skilled Technology teams to deliver against rapidly changing business requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of our London-based Infrastructure and Platform Engineering team, this position supports our multi-tenant private and public cloud initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role contributes to the delivery of services to our core business areas globally, including Trading, middle and back office, and Technology. The role requires an understanding of platforms including Windows, virtualisation and their associated technologies, delivered through on-premises, hosted and public cloud environments. It involves system integration, support and continuous improvement, with an emphasis on standardisation, repeatability, automation and orchestration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will cover BAU rota activities alongside business project initiatives. We are looking for a proactive self-starter who can manage their workload, identify opportunities for improvement and work alongside senior engineers to develop their experience in solution design, scoping and architecture across our key technology platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With the team’s broad technology remit, this role would suit someone early in their Windows platform engineering career who is keen to build their experience in a fast-paced environment and gain exposure to a wide range of technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 5 years of industry experience. Prior experience in a similar role within a Financial institution will be advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive platform engineering and support experience biased towards the Microsoft server technology portfolio, including On-premise bare metal hardware deployments (preferably HPE), Advanced virtualisation design, architecture and support across VMware and Microsoft Hyper-V platforms, together with container technologies such as Kubernetes. This should also include enterprise integration experience with security, high availability, networking, load balancing aspects to deliver applications and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering Microsoft 365 services including Exchange Online, Entra ID, Teams and SharePoint Online.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and proficiency in translating requirements through to providing and supporting solutions and environments for both proprietary and commercial software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform engineering and support experience with public cloud platforms, preferably with a major Hyperscaler like Microsoft Azure or AWS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Infrastructure as Code methodologies with On-Prem and Cloud IaaS, achieved through automation and orchestration of cross-platform services using tools such as Source Control, Ansible, Jenkins, Terraform and ServiceNow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable scripting or programming skills in languages such as PowerShell, Python and familiarity with APIs and data structures in JSON/YAML or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GenAI technologies via Public Cloud, OpenAI, AWS, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is analytical and methodical, with a proven track record in problem-solving, critical BAU, advanced engineering and technology service delivery in a high-pressure, time-sensitive environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should be passionate about emerging technology trends, innovations and directions, and eager to suggest and implement new solutions to enhance our technology performance. You should also understand the need for rapid delivery while appreciating business risk and constraints to ensure adherence to service levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The candidate should have experience working both independently and as part of a diverse team, meeting both broad and specific project/BAU objectives. This role requires excellent organisational skills, open communication, and a collaborative approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your commitment to continuous improvement should be evident, both in learning from others and sharing knowledge to enhance our team&#39;s capability and function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;BlueCrest is committed to providing an inclusive environment for its workforce. As an employer, we provide equal opportunities to all people regardless of their gender, marital or civil partnership status, race, religion or ethnicity, disability, age, sexual orientation or nationality. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Technology Infrastructure team operates globally and is responsible for every aspect of the firm&#39;s hybrid platform. This ranges from our EUC/Office environments to Trading and Core service Co-Location Data Centres, and extends to Public Cloud, delivering top-tier technology services to a dynamic and demanding Trading organisation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In addition to meeting the round-the-clock operational demands of the platforms, we continuously evolve and transform our platforms to maintain a competitive edge that our business requires. We innovate to provide valuable solutions and leverage our skilled Technology teams to deliver against rapidly changing business requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI DevOps Engineer is a very technical, hands-on role, responsible for end to end delivery and operations of our DevOps environments. They will be joining the team as we lead an ambitious technology modernisation journey, moving to greater adoption of AI, microservices and public cloud. We’re continuing to evolve our global infrastructure - spanning multiple global data centres - into a modern hybrid architecture that leverages both existing on-prem and multi-cloud environments and capabilities across Azure and AWS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the past four years, we&#39;ve modernised our core trading systems and introduced a range of key technologies including AI, Kubernetes, Kafka, ELK, Prometheus, and more. As we expand and enhance the platforms, our focus is on automating and standardising to ensure consistency, scalability and reliability across all environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experiences and Skills Required:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong object oriented Python skills (not just scripting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent understanding of containerisation technologies, ideally Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with GitHub Actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC):
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good, enterprise experience with Terragrunt, Terraform, and Ansible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivery-focused mindset, with priorities aligned to business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have, but willing to learn otherwise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and deploying AI agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise across Azure and AWS, with a solid understanding of AI-native services:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Azure AI Foundry and Amazon Bedrock&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud automation experienceAgentOps/DataOps frameworks (e.g. LangGraph, Dagster) and OpenTelemetry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Predictive operations tools (e.g. Prophet, Dynatrace)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI tool integration, including embedding LLM APIs and agents into pipelinesExperience integrating DevOps infrastructure with MCPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure testing frameworks (Terratest, Terraform Test, Molecule, JUnit, pytest)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kubernetes engineering and support across on-prem, VMware, AKS and EKS environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Linux and Windows administration and network automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Java and/or C# troubleshooting capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD experience with GitHub Actions and/or TeamCity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Artifact repository management (Nexus, Artifactory)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability, monitoring and tracing (OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, ELK, Tempo, Jaeger)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform engineering on Azure and/or AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data platform experience (Kafka, Redis)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chaos engineering and resilience testing (Gremlin, LitmusChaos)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a very strong individual contributor who is passionate about emerging technologies. You’ll need to be comfortable working in a very dynamic, fast-paced environment. Enabling the business is our number one priority – this means working on any part of the delivery stack, from routine o/s IaC, to documentation, instrumentation all the way to automating work through Python microservices or LangChain based agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should be passionate about AI and other emerging technology trends, innovations and directions, and eager to suggest and implement new solutions to enhance our technology performance. You should also understand the need for rapid delivery while appreciating business risk and constraints to ensure adherence to service levels.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The candidate should have extensive experience working both independently and as part of a diverse team, meeting both broad and specific project/BAU objectives. This role requires excellent organisational skills, open communication, and a collaborative approach.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your commitment to continuous improvement should be evident, both in learning from others and sharing knowledge to enhance our team&#39;s capability and function.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;BlueCrest is committed to providing an inclusive environment for its workforce. As an employer, we provide equal opportunities to all people regardless of their gender, marital or civil partnership status, race, religion or ethnicity, disability, age, sexual orientation or nationality. &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Affirm, we exist for the moments that matter—giving people a clear, predictable way to pay over time, with no hidden fees, no surprises, and no tradeoffs on what matters most.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;Affirm is reinventing credit to make it more honest and friendly, giving consumers the flexibility to buy now and pay later without any hidden fees or compounding interest. Our mission to deliver honest financial products that improve lives extends beyond borders. Consumers across the globe need safe, transparent financing. Our retail partners need Affirm to be there for them, wherever that might be. To help achieve this vision, we are expanding our product lines and becoming a global company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The International Consumer product team is responsible for building and scaling Affirm’s direct-to-consumer products and experiences across international markets. This includes our apps, wallets, marketplace, and related offerings that help consumers discover, use, and manage Affirm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Product Manager on the International Consumer team, you will drive the strategy, execution, and growth of Affirm’s direct-to-consumer products across international markets – from iterating on the product vision, refining the product strategy, developing a roadmap, and leading execution.&lt;br&gt;In this role, you will work closely with a broad set of cross functional teams across the entire business, as well as a number of engineering teams. Effective stakeholder management and ability to successfully navigate organizational dynamics are a must for success. You should be commercially minded, be high agency with a bias towards action, and comfortable having technical conversations (and opinions).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive the execution, growth, and scale of Affirm’s consumer products and experiences across international markets&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Take Affirm’s direct-to-consumer products and adapt them for international markets by understanding consumer needs, analyzing performance data, and iterating on the product’s features and capabilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive success metrics by shipping high impact work that meaningfully moves the needle for Affirm’s business and customers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner effectively with engineering teams across the organization to drive product development and prioritization&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders (such as Design, Research, Analytics, Marketing, Legal, Compliance, Credit, Fraud, etc.) to shape your product roadmap and incorporate legal, governance, and regulatory oversight into your products&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Understand Affirm’s international consumers at a deep level: what’s important to them, what drives their decision making, why they love Affirm, and what they wish we could do better&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify and create the experiences that make it seamless for consumers to discover, use, and manage Affirm across our apps, wallets, marketplace, and related direct-to-consumer offerings&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Look For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This isn’t your first rodeo. You’ve directly managed technical software products from kick-off to post-launch – driving meaningful business impact that you can speak to&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have experience working on consumer technology products in Canada, UK, EU, or Australia (bonus points if that experience is in fintech, commerce, marketplaces, or payments)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re equally comfortable diving into technical details with an engineer, iterating on a Figma with a designer, and breaking down a funnel with a data analyst&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have the discipline, organizational skills, and interpersonal communication skills necessary to navigate complex organizational dynamics – you have specific examples of times when you’ve secured a decision from a broad group of senior stakeholders&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ve worked in an environment where you were reliant on engineering teams outside of your direct purview and were able to effectively influence them to prioritize and build what you needed for your product&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re the kind of person who cares about getting things done. You have a bias towards action and can effectively navigate obstacles and blockers&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can turn incomplete, conflicting, or ambiguous inputs into a solid action plan&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have direct experience shipping high-quality products on time&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You feel comfortable jumping into the commercial aspects of product development – you’re able to connect customer needs, product decisions, and business outcomes, and make clear tradeoffs across them&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Grade - N&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity Grade - 5&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Employees new to Affirm typically come in at the start of the pay range. Affirm focuses on providing a simple and transparent pay structure which is based on a variety of factors, including location, experience and job-related skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base pay is part of a total compensation package that may include monthly stipends for health, wellness and tech spending, and benefits (including 100% subsidized medical coverage, dental and vision for you and your dependents). In addition, the employees may be eligible for equity rewards offered by Affirm Holdings, Inc. (parent company).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;GBR base pay range per year: &amp;nbsp;£120,000–£168,000 GBP&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location - Remote UK&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;#LI-Remote&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Remote-first with flexibility built in&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Affirm is proud to be a remote-first company. Most roles can be done from almost anywhere within the country of employment. Some positions may occasionally require in-person work at an Affirm office, and a few are office-based due to the nature of the work. All new hires will be invited to attend an in-person onboarding experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits designed for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our benefits reflect our commitment to care, transparency, and flexibility. Here are a few highlights:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health coverage at no cost: We cover 100% of premiums for employees and their dependents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spending stipends: Monthly stipends support your tech setup, and the ability to choose health and wellness options that are right for you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time off to recharge: Flexible time off and generous holiday calendars help you rest when you need to.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a piece of what you build: Our employee stock purchase plan (ESPP) lets you buy Affirm stock at a discount.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re committed to providing an inclusive interview process, including accommodations for candidates with disabilities. If you need support, we’re happy to help.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For positions based in San Francisco or Los Angeles: Affirm considers qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By clicking &quot;Submit Application,&quot; you acknowledge that you have read Affirm&#39;s&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.affirm.com/global-candidate-privacy-notice&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and consent to the use of your personal information as described.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Twilio, we’re shaping the future of communications, all from the comfort of our homes. We deliver innovative solutions to&lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://customers.twilio.com/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;hundreds of thousands of businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;and empower millions of developers worldwide to craft personalized customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our dedication to &lt;a class=&quot;c-link&quot; href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/en-us/blog/open-work&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;remote-first work&lt;/a&gt;, and strong culture of connection and global inclusion means that no matter your location, you’re part of a vibrant team with diverse experiences making a global impact each day. As we continue to revolutionize how the world interacts, we’re acquiring new skills and experiences that make work feel truly rewarding. Your career at Twilio is in your hands.&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hiring and how we work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use Artificial Intelligence (AI) to help make our hiring process efficient. That said, every hiring decision is made by real Twilions!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Also, while we are a remote-first company, you may be asked to report in person on an ad-hoc basis for team gatherings, functional off-sites or customer meetings.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;See yourself at Twilio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the team as Twilio’s next New Business Account Executive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is needed to sell into high value Enterprise prospects and existing customers with ARR over $25k. You will play a key role in further growing Twilio’s Communication Products business across the DACH&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Region. You will be responsible for sourcing new, high value customers as well as driving the sales process from internal leads to qualifying new prospects and handling deals to closure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be responsible for new customer acquisition and driving ACV for a specific set of accounts while maintaining the highest levels of customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master creating pricing proposals, negotiating terms and managing the contract process. Ideally, you also have experience selling communications to a technical and business audience, building trust and mutual respect with technical customers and peers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be passionate about what you do and you are able to think outside of the box and have extraordinary interpersonal and communication skills to make complex contractual, technical, and financial details sound simple.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to balance challenging priorities and handle multiple projects/deals at the same time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Twilio values diverse experiences from all kinds of industries, and we encourage everyone who meets the required qualifications to apply. If your career is just starting or hasn&#39;t followed a traditional path, don&#39;t let that stop you from considering Twilio. We are always looking for people who will bring something new to the table!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;*Required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of Enterprise Sales experience and a track record of personally selling and closing complex solutions to enterprise and software companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience identifying, mapping and prospecting enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in selling complex, technical solutions such as cloud communications platforms, APIs, and/or enterprise software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in account management, developing and managing large enterprise clients, and a history of meeting or exceeding sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Fortune 500 or similarly large enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in working within a quota-driven environment with proven ability to close high-value deals (e.g., six to seven figures)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in solution-based selling or consultative selling&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation and contract management skills, including handling complex deals with long sales cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospecting and lead generation skills—ability to develop a pipeline through multiple channels, including direct sales, partnerships, and networking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build and nurture relationships with C-level executives, decision-makers, cross-functional partners and key stakeholders in large enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation and negotiation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a dynamic environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: bold;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in German&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally, you also have experience selling both to a business and technical audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the CPaaS ecosystem and familiarity with:&amp;nbsp;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud communications (voice, SMS, chat, video, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APIs and integrations for communication services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Telecommunications industry dynamics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of enterprise technology architecture and the technical needs of large organizations, including how CPaaS solutions integrate with existing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be remote, and based in UK, Spain or Ireland.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We prioritize connection and opportunities to build relationships with our customers and each other. For this role, approximately 25% travel is anticipated to help you connect in-person in a meaningful way.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working at Twilio offers many benefits, including competitive pay, generous time off, ample parental and wellness leave, healthcare, a retirement savings program, and much more. Offerings vary by location.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio thinks big. Do you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We like to solve problems, take initiative, pitch in when needed, and are always up for trying new things. That&#39;s why we seek out colleagues who embody our values — something we call &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/values&quot;&gt;Twilio Magic&lt;/a&gt;. Additionally, we empower employees to build &lt;a href=&quot;https://twilio.org/support-and-resources/impact-fund&quot;&gt;positive change in their communities&lt;/a&gt; by supporting their volunteering and donation efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;So, if you&#39;re ready to unleash your full potential, do your best work, and be the best version of yourself, apply now! If this role isn&#39;t what you&#39;re looking for, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.twilio.com/company/jobs#open-positions&quot;&gt;please consider other open positions.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay alert to recruitment fraud&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We care about your safety. Scammers sometimes impersonate Twilio recruiters through fake job postings, emails, websites, or messages. Please ensure you are engaging with an official @&lt;a href=&quot;http://twilio.com&quot;&gt;twilio.com&lt;/a&gt; email address. We will never ask for payment, gift cards, cryptocurrency, or banking information during the recruiting process. We do not make job offers without a formal interview process or conduct interviews exclusively through text-based messaging apps.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Twilio is proud to be an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/strong&gt; We do not discriminate based upon race, religion, color, national origin, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, reproductive health decisions, or related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, status as a protected veteran, status as an individual with a disability, genetic information, political views or activity, or other applicable legally protected characteristics. We also consider qualified applicants with criminal histories, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law. Qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records will be considered for employment in accordance with the Los Angeles County Fair Chance Ordinance for Employers and the California Fair Chance Act. Additionally, Twilio participates in the E-Verify program in certain locations, as required by law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;Duetto&#39;s platform runs 24/7 for hotels, resorts, and casinos around the world, and that reliability doesn&#39;t happen by accident. We&#39;re looking for a Senior DevOps Engineer to architect, build, and own the AWS infrastructure that keeps our Revenue &amp;amp; Profit Operating System fast, secure, and always on, while helping shape how our engineering org automates its way out of manual toil.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes Us Different?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Duetto is the hospitality industry&#39;s leading revenue management platform, founded in 2012 by former Wynn Resorts executives who knew the industry needed better technology. We built the world&#39;s first Revenue &amp;amp; Profit Operating System — a suite of tools (GameChanger, ScoreBoard, BlockBuster, Advance and more) that goes beyond room pricing to give hotels, resorts and casinos a complete picture of their revenue and profitability. Trusted by clients ranging from independent boutique hotels to global chains, we&#39;ve been named the #1 Revenue Management Software by HotelTechAwards four years running and the #1 Best Place to Work in Hotel Tech in 2025. Backed by GrowthCurve Capital since 2024, we&#39;re accelerating our investment in AI, and we&#39;re genuinely passionate about the industry we serve. We build products we&#39;re proud of, for customers we care about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect and implement infrastructure for seamless migrations of critical systems, keeping uptime and reliability front and center&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain the tooling and processes that let our SaaS products scale and run themselves on AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with developers to strengthen the reliability, performance, security, and scalability of our application architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the critical infrastructure components that keep everything highly available and secure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment across technical and non-technical teams, making sure infrastructure decisions serve the whole business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take your turn as last line of defense in our weekly on-call rotation, leading root cause analysis and driving fixes that stick for good&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you have the following:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in an Ops, DevOps, or SRE role, with real system design and architecture chops. You&#39;re comfortable administering cloud infrastructure hands-on (AWS preferred, Azure or GCP also welcome), and you know your way around networking and security at an engineering level.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re fluent in the AWS ecosystem (IAM, VPC, EC2, ELB, RDS, S3, Lambda, API Gateway, Secrets Manager, KMS, CloudWatch, CloudTrail), have run Terraform/Terragrunt in production, and have worked with Chef or Puppet.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re at home with GitHub, GitHub Actions, Jenkins, JFrog Artifactory, and GitOps workflows, and you&#39;ve used DataDog, Prometheus, or Grafana to keep tabs on system health.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can read Java, Ruby, Bash/Zsh, HCL, Python, and JavaScript well enough to move fast across a codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ECS or EKS, exposure to SOC2 or secure-by-default practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with L7 load balancing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Duetto?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll own meaningful infrastructure decisions, not just execute someone else&#39;s blueprint. New tooling choices are proposed with a business case and decided as a team, so your judgment matters&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We&#39;re an AI-forward company across every function, not just engineering. You&#39;ll be equipped to use AI for things like incident triage, IaC code generation, and runbook authoring, and encouraged to push that further&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ll work at the intersection of serious infrastructure and an industry we genuinely love. Our customers depend on us around the clock, and that shows up in how seriously we take reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real collaboration, not silos. You&#39;ll partner directly with developers and cross-functional teams to solve problems together, not just file tickets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We celebrate diverse perspectives and back that up with the room to debate ideas openly. Come as you are, and bring your full self to the work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Location: Remote, Croatia, Spain or UK&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work model: Fully remote&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weekly on-call rotation as last line of support for 24/7 services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Duetto is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, colour, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sound like you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If this sounds like the kind of infrastructure work that gets you excited, apply even if you don&#39;t check every single box. We&#39;d rather meet someone with the right instincts and hunger to grow than tick boxes on a checklist.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job title:&lt;/strong&gt; Principal Engineer&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;London / Bristol / Edinburgh&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team:&lt;/strong&gt; Enterprise Architecture&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary:&lt;/strong&gt; £120,000 - £160,000&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting to:&lt;/strong&gt; Director of Enterprise Architecture&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role is based in London, Bristol or Edinburgh&amp;nbsp;and requires existing right to work in the UK.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;At this time, we are not able to offer visa sponsorship for this role. We are committed to building a diverse, global team and our sponsorship policy is evaluated on a role-by-role basis. We encourage you to keep an eye on our careers site to stay informed about future opportunities where we are able to offer visa sponsorship.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kaluza is the Energy Intelligence Platform, turning energy complexity into seamless coordination. We help energy companies overcome today’s challenges while accelerating the shift to a clean, electrified future.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our platform orchestrates millions of real-time decisions across homes, devices, markets and grids. By combining predictive algorithms with human-centred design, Kaluza makes clean energy dependable, affordable and adaptive to everyday life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;With teams across Europe, Asia and Australia, and a joint venture with Mitsubishi Corporation in Japan, we power leading companies including OVO, AGL and ENGIE, as well as innovators like Volvo and Volkswagen.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;303&quot; data-local-id=&quot;71635837-a0ff-40e4-8b75-a1ff2b4444d0&quot;&gt;As a Principal Software Engineer at Kaluza, you will be the leading technical authority for a major global product area comprising multiple modules. You will lead innovation on some of the most complex, ambiguous, and large-scale solutions, aligning them with target architecture standards and contributing to the creation of a scalable platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;651&quot; data-local-id=&quot;afe318c5-d169-4335-980d-c55899c830d5&quot;&gt;You’ll have a broad sphere of influence, enabling multiple teams and serving as a strategic partner to our architecture leadership team and our community of principal and staff engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;840&quot; data-local-id=&quot;5d1958d8-2004-4ea0-821c-a0ebcadb4a0e&quot;&gt;Your impact will come mostly from &#39;hands-off&#39; work; you’ll not be expected to write code day-to-day. But for some challenges, you may need to dive into code-level design or help build a proof-of-concept.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ideally you’ll have/be&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1072&quot; data-local-id=&quot;c232f15f-f0a4-4008-a7b5-f91f1cfafc20&quot;&gt;Architect modern distributed, cloud-based systems applying modern architecture and engineering practices in an enterprise software environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1219&quot; data-local-id=&quot;8dba6a70-6d5c-45e2-a3af-1ccdaa41a861&quot;&gt;Shape and influence technical vision and product roadmaps to align with business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1310&quot; data-local-id=&quot;562ddf14-2519-461d-9844-e47621078721&quot;&gt;Provide hands-on leadership, making appropriate technical choices to satisfy requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1404&quot; data-local-id=&quot;7a0244ae-b45c-4845-88d4-50316da986b9&quot;&gt;Mentor and guide engineers in delivering autonomous, loosely coupled distributed systems with proven architectural principles and patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1547&quot; data-local-id=&quot;77346099-2aa3-43c1-91d9-749290fea5e1&quot;&gt;Lead technical due diligence and make high-stakes decisions with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1627&quot; data-local-id=&quot;7e1a1e9f-a262-4aec-8e83-9332f726304a&quot;&gt;Deliver results, influence diverse audiences, and orchestrate cross-functional solutions spanning multiple product features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1755&quot; data-local-id=&quot;c409df9a-e0b3-4f6b-a9a3-39d995612adf&quot;&gt;Engage effectively with both technical teams and executive leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1826&quot; data-local-id=&quot;7cb74d57-f395-456f-b7cf-298b271ed930&quot;&gt;Work independently and collaboratively, bringing strong opinions while respecting others, communicating openly, and maintaining self-awareness with a continuous growth mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What will set you apart&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2035&quot; data-local-id=&quot;a0dbc1d1-8544-470c-ae8a-18a2b9c5f141&quot;&gt;Experience enabling engineering teams to use AI and delivering AI/ML powered solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2126&quot; data-local-id=&quot;4e471dc5-7261-4e8c-ad4b-265e11f79d54&quot;&gt;Demonstrable experience in architecting solutions in complex business domains, particularly interface design and data modelling, ideally with experience in AWS and API design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2305&quot; data-local-id=&quot;1d87f974-8329-4a1b-9b26-2dfa45af34f8&quot;&gt;Proven track record delivering global &lt;span data-highlighted=&quot;true&quot; data-vc=&quot;highlighted-text&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_1mT5xdRAKS&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;_0nmozVaHVx _2V7sgO2M4S _3BoeIDwZ7G _30zrXRyxdf _0ReiIH7zJH&quot; data-testid=&quot;definition-highlighter&quot;&gt;B2B2C&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt; SaaS (energy or other mission‑critical industries).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2404&quot; data-local-id=&quot;769f5e5e-483c-4ef8-ba0e-ff433059a8a0&quot;&gt;Success driving adoption of modern engineering practices (e.g. DevOps, CI/CD).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2486&quot; data-local-id=&quot;d6312d22-3a41-4bcc-837e-9eee49ca8fda&quot;&gt;Experience leading teams through significant changes in ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;2562&quot; data-local-id=&quot;f6f5546f-363b-4985-91fd-d58666e49784&quot;&gt;Ability to ramp up rapidly in new domains and technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you&#39;ll work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We offer flexible working, with an expectation of 3 days a week in the office. This gives us the best of both: real time together to collaborate and build relationships, with the flexibility to work in the way that suits you best the rest of the week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kaluza Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Here at Kaluza we have five core values that guide us as a business: Play to win, Solve the real problem, Build trust every day, Own the outcome, Go further together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary Bonus Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance + Virtual GP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life Assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to Furthr - a Climate Action app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free Mortgage Advice and Eye Tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perks at Work - access to thousands of retail discounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5% Flex Fund - to spend on the benefits you want most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;26 days holiday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progressive Leave Policy - With no qualifying service periods, including 26 weeks full pay if you have a new addition to your family&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal Learning Budget - Upskill, learn and grow!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Home Office Budget&lt;br&gt;And more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want the best people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re keen to meet people from all walks of life — our view is that the more inclusive we are, the better our work will be. We want to build teams which represent a variety of experiences, perspectives and skills, and we recognise talent on the basis of merit and potential.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We understand some people may not apply for jobs unless they tick every box. But if you&#39;re excited about joining us and think you have some of what we&#39;re looking for, even if you&#39;re not 100% sure, we&#39;d still love to hear from you.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Find out more about working in&lt;a href=&quot;http://kaluza.com/&quot;&gt; Kaluza&lt;/a&gt; on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://kaluza-dev.webflow.io/careers&quot;&gt; careers page&lt;/a&gt; and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/kaluza/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Shape how Graphcore products move from hardware design into reliable volume manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Staff Manufacturing Product Engineer, you will take a leading role in supporting NPI development and volume production across complex hardware products. You will connect design, test, quality and supply chain decisions with real manufacturing outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Your work will help ensure products are manufacturable, resilient and ready for supplier capability. You will provide DfM feedback that improves PCB and system design before issues reach production.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;You will work closely with contract manufacturers, especially during NPI and early volume manufacture. You will drive yield improvement, analyse production data and resolve L6 manufacturing issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This role suits someone who enjoys practical engineering ownership across design and production. You will travel to Taiwan and work close to suppliers shaping next generation manufacturing technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The team and culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join the Manufacturing and Technology Process team within Operations. The team works across Bristol, Cambridge and Taiwan, close to foundry, package assembly and PCBA partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work happens through clear ownership, supplier engagement and fast feedback into design teams. You will speak up early when manufacturability, yield or capability needs attention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team values evidence, responsibility and strong cross-regional relationships. Decisions are made through engineering judgement, data and direct accountability for manufacturing performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Strong fault diagnosis, problem solving and failure analysis skills, including ICT to SMT debug&lt;br&gt;· Thorough understanding of Automated surface mount assembly processes and manufacturing methodologies&lt;br&gt;· Working knowledge of L10 mechanical design and system build, ideally for HPC products&lt;br&gt;· Ability to connect silicon, package and PCB interactions into clear DfM feedback&lt;br&gt;· Experienced in statistical analysis tools (e.g JMP, SQL, Python)&lt;br&gt;· Experience using continuous improvement methods, including SPC and DOE&lt;br&gt;· Strong interpersonal skills for supplier-facing, cross-functional and cross-regional engineering work&lt;br&gt;· Extensive experience in a similar manufacturing facing role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;While we have outlined a set of requirements, we value transferable skills and diverse experiences. If you meet most of our essential criteria, we encourage you to submit an application and showcase how your background makes you a strong candidate.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;· Flexible working: Balance your work and personal life with greater flexibility&lt;br&gt;· Generous leave: Take time to rest, recharge and enjoy life outside of work&lt;br&gt;· Retirement planning support: Up to 5% matched pension&lt;br&gt;· Phantom equity: Share in Graphcore’s success&lt;br&gt;· Workplace experience: Enjoy thoughtfully designed office spaces for collaboration, with free food and an on-site barista to support your day&lt;br&gt;· Peace of mind protection: Income protection and life assurance to provide financial security for you and your loved ones&lt;br&gt;· Flexible benefits: Tailor your benefits package with a choice of additional options, including private medical insurance and dental cover&lt;br&gt;· Optional benefits: Dental cover, health cash plan, private medical insurance, cycle to work scheme, give as you earn&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome people from all backgrounds and experiences and are committed to building an inclusive environment where everyone can do their best work.&lt;br&gt;We’re an equal opportunity employer and recognise that everyone brings different strengths and perspectives. If you need any adjustments during the interview process, just let us know - we’re happy to support you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sponsorship&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must have the legal right to work in the UK. Unfortunately, we are unable to provide visa sponsorship or support visa applications for this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Join the Team at Graphcore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore is one of the world’s leading innovators in Artificial Intelligence compute. It is developing hardware, software and systems infrastructure that will unlock the next generation of AI breakthroughs and power the widespread adoption of AI solutions across every industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the SoftBank Group, Graphcore is a member of an elite family of companies responsible for some of the world’s most transformative technologies. Together, they share a bold vision: to enable Artificial Super Intelligence and ensure its benefits are accessible to everyone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Graphcore’s teams are drawn from diverse backgrounds and bring a broad range of skills and perspectives. A melting pot of AI research specialists, silicon designers, software engineers and systems architects, Graphcore brings together deep expertise to solve complex problems and deliver meaningful progress in AI compute.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you want to turn hardware design into stronger manufacturing performance, we’d love to hear from you. Apply now to help shape how Graphcore products are built.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Fanatics Markets:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Markets is the real-money prediction and trading app where you can invest in moments you care about. Built on a secure platform, we let users predict real-world outcomes and trade on events they actually follow — from sports and entertainment to political elections and beyond. Our mission is to redefine how fans engage with the moments and markets that matter most. We&#39;re looking for the right people to help us build the future of prediction markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This Staff Software Engineer role is an individual contributor position with technical leadership and significant ownership across our full stack: the web application customers use to interact with our product and the backend systems that power it. You&#39;ll combine hands-on engineering with responsibility for shaping architecture, setting technical direction, and enabling engineers across teams to deliver effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Whether your deepest expertise is in frontend or backend engineering, you&#39;ll apply that strength across the platform while making meaningful contributions on the other side of the stack. Joining a product at an exciting early stage, you&#39;ll help define its technical foundations, identify the highest-impact engineering challenges, and turn ambiguous problems into clear plans that balance customer needs, delivery speed, and long-term reliability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your impact will extend beyond the systems you build. You&#39;ll lead complex initiatives spanning teams, mentor engineers, and establish practices that improve engineering quality and effectiveness. You&#39;ll also shape our approach to AI-assisted development while building systems that can handle millions of events daily.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the engineering side, we&#39;re pioneering the use of AI as a code collaborator. We need engineers who have gone beyond experimentation — who actively use Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot, or similar tools to ship production code faster while maintaining exceptional quality standards, and who can help others adopt these workflows responsibly and effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction for major areas of the Markets platform, aligning architectural decisions with product strategy and guiding their implementation across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of complex, scalable systems and customer experiences, contributing hands-on in React, Next.js, and TypeScript or backend services in Go, while making meaningful contributions across the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve ambiguous engineering problems spanning team or system boundaries, turning them into clear proposals, delivery plans, and measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own critical initiatives end-to-end, from discovery and technical specifications through implementation, instrumentation, deployment, monitoring, and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product, design, platform, and infrastructure teams to make informed tradeoffs across customer experience, accessibility, performance, security, reliability, and delivery speed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define architecture and integration patterns for frontend applications, backend APIs, and event-driven systems, with particular attention to correctness in markets, orders, and transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide the design of experimentation capabilities, including feature flags and A/B tests, so teams can validate ideas quickly and safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate scaling constraints, reliability risks, and technical debt; build alignment on pragmatic improvements and drive them through to completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise engineering standards through design reviews, code reviews, testing strategies, observability, and safe deployment practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and develop technical leaders, helping teams make sound decisions and solve problems independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and evolve standards for AI-assisted development, including appropriate use cases, review expectations, security safeguards, and validation strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure and improve engineering effectiveness, sharing tools and practices that increase delivery speed without compromising quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead through influence in an early-stage product environment, creating clarity, unblocking teams, and establishing ways of working that support growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantial experience building and operating highly scalable production systems, with demonstrated impact at Staff level or equivalent scope, including technical leadership across teams or major platform areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in either user-facing web applications built with JavaScript/TypeScript and React or backend services built with languages such as Go, Java, or Python, alongside the ability to reason across the full stack. If you&#39;re frontend-strong, you don&#39;t need to arrive fluent in Go, but you should be comfortable engaging with backend architecture and system tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting technical direction and delivering complex initiatives from ambiguous requirements through to measurable production outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architectural judgment, including the ability to assess tradeoffs, establish clear system boundaries, and evolve systems as product requirements and scale change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping React architecture, component-driven development, and modern state management using tools such as Next.js, TanStack Query, Tailwind, or Zustand; or deep backend experience with data modeling, distributed systems, and event-driven architecture using technologies such as Postgres and Kafka/PubSub&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of your primary language&#39;s features, idioms, and best practices, with experience establishing standards adopted beyond your immediate team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of performance, reliability, and security, including responsive design and accessibility on the frontend or scalability, observability, data integrity, and failure handling on the backend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining API contracts and collaborating across product, platform, and infrastructure teams to deliver reliable systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping CI/CD pipelines, testing strategies, and safe deployment practices across services or applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead through influence, build alignment across teams, and communicate technical decisions clearly to engineers and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of mentoring engineers, strengthening technical decision-making, and increasing the effectiveness of others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience using AI tools such as Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, or Copilot to ship production code, with sound judgment about their limitations and appropriate validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specific examples of improving development workflows, with evidence of their impact on delivery speed, quality, or engineering productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team-first approach, with the judgment to move between strategic technical work and hands-on delivery according to the needs of the product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create clarity in a high-growth environment where priorities evolve and decisions must be made quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, including experience aligning teams and navigating dependencies within large enterprise environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;You don&#39;t need to tick every box — deep strength in one area, demonstrated technical leadership, and a willingness to learn go a long way.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience shaping technical foundations in early-stage or high-growth startup environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-money transaction systems, including financial correctness, auditability, and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing technical roadmaps or leading architectural changes adopted across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in building developer tools or improving engineering productivity at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing AI-assisted engineering practices across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributions to open-source projects or the technical community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc in Computer Science or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Depending on the role, your interview and onboarding experience may include in-person components, such as onsite interviews or Launching into Better: LIVE—a multi-day cultural immersion in New York City for full-time, non-seasonal hires. These sessions are designed to build connections and bring our culture to life, though specific travel and participation requirements will be confirmed based on your role and location. Your recruiter will provide clear guidance at each stage of the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to build the future of sports trading? If you possess some of these skills but not all of them, we still encourage you to apply! Please note that visa sponsorship is not available for this position. We are open to fully remote candidates based in the United Kingdom. Remote employees may also be eligible for a home office setup stipend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.organization-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our &lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Soho, London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid working: 3 days in the office Tues - Thurs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To provide technical leadership and hands-on contribution within a data engineering team, designing, building, and optimizing robust data pipelines and infrastructure for a global sports betting and media business. This role is crucial in delivering high-quality data solutions that support LiveScore’s strategic goals and embody our commitment to being Fan Driven and a Champion of Sport. You will mentor junior engineers and ensure technical excellence in your domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At LiveScore Group, we’re the proud home of three of the most exciting brands in the sports and gaming world: LiveScore, LiveScore Bet and Virgin Bet. A fully owned and operated ecosystem that converges the two worlds of sports media and sports betting. We’re proud of the high ratings for our commitment to excellence and fueling fan’s passion for sport driving us to the top.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don’t just lead; we innovate. Our cutting-edge products and immersive experiences set the standard, but it’s our people who truly make the difference. Every day, our team embody our values: adaptability, teamwork, a fan-driven approach, and an ever-curious mindset that fuels our ambition. As we scale and continue to create a culture that allows all employees to thrive, we know we need the most talented people with diverse backgrounds, perspectives and skills. If you’re good at what you do, come and join us. The more inclusive we are, the more amazing experiences we can create for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We know that job descriptions can sometimes seem daunting, and you might not feel you tick every box. But, if you’re passionate about the role and have relevant experience, we want to hear from you!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership and Guidance:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as a primary technical point of contact and subject matter expert for specific data engineering projects or domains, guiding team members through complex technical challenges and promoting innovative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Data Solution Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Design, develop, test, and deploy highly scalable, reliable, and fault-tolerant data pipelines and ETL/ELT processes. This includes data ingestion from diverse sources, data transformation, and data loading into various data stores (e.g., data warehouses, data lakes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architectural Implementation:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with Data Architects to translate architectural blueprints and standards into concrete implementations, ensuring new data components align with the overall data strategy and infrastructure requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentorship and Skill Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively mentor and coach junior and mid-level data engineers, providing constructive feedback, sharing technical knowledge, and fostering their growth in coding, data modeling, and general data engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-On Contribution:&lt;/strong&gt; Maintain a significant hands-on role in coding, data modeling, infrastructure-as-code development, and platform configuration, leading by example and ensuring high-quality output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality and Performance Assurance:&lt;/strong&gt; Take direct responsibility for ensuring the quality, integrity, and performance of data assets within their assigned domain or projects, implementing monitoring, validation, and optimization strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Efficiency and Cost Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt; Proactively identify and implement technical optimizations for data processing, storage, and infrastructure utilization to improve efficiency, reduce operational costs, and enhance system performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code Review and Best Practices:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead and participate in rigorous code reviews, advocating for and enforcing engineering best practices, coding standards, and architectural patterns to maintain high code quality and system stability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Problem Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Diagnose, troubleshoot, and provide effective solutions for highly complex data-related issues, incidents, and performance bottlenecks, often working under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate effectively with other engineering teams, product managers, data scientists, and business stakeholders to understand data requirements, integrate solutions, and provide technical insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Knowledge and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced Data Pipeline Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven, in-depth experience as a senior or lead data engineer with a strong portfolio of hands-on contributions to designing, building, and optimizing complex, large-scale data pipelines and ETL/ELT processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Data Warehousing (EDW) and Data Modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong practical experience with EDW concepts, principles, and implementation, specifically including the design and practical application of a single, integrated data model for analytical purposes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud Data Platforms:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with cloud-native data services and infrastructure on at least one major cloud provider (e.g., AWS services like S3, Redshift, Glue, EMR; GCP services like BigQuery, Dataflow, Pub/Sub; Azure services like Data Lake, Synapse Analytics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cost Optimization Strategies:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to identify, propose, and implement technical solutions that lead to significant cost savings in data processing, storage, and infrastructure within a large-scale data environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Engineering Fundamentals:&lt;/strong&gt; Expert proficiency in software development methodologies (e.g., Agile, Scrum), version control (Git), CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, and comprehensive understanding of software engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Programming Languages:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional coding skills in at least one relevant programming language (e.g., Python, Scala, Java, JavaScript, C/C++), with a focus on writing clean, efficient, and maintainable code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Database Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Extensive experience with various database technologies including relational databases (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL), NoSQL databases (e.g., MongoDB, Cassandra), and analytical data warehouses (e.g., Snowflake, Redshift, BigQuery).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Architecture Principles:&lt;/strong&gt; Solid understanding of data architecture patterns (e.g., Data Mesh, Data Lakehouse, Lambda/Kappa architectures), distributed systems, and their practical application.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Practical experience in developing and maintaining robust and auditable data solutions for regulatory reporting, particularly within the gaming or other highly regulated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluent in AI prompting alongside staying ahead of emerging AI technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership &amp;amp; Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; A natural leader who can effectively guide, inspire, and technically mentor junior and mid-level engineers. Possesses the ability to break down complex problems, provide clear direction, and foster a learning environment, thereby enhancing team capabilities and promoting adherence to best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
